{"kind":"report","text":"approved: independent Architecture/Security/Simplification review of exact head 85bb57b0c396c81f488a7acb457467cad6d1d887 on branch request/custody-lost-update-current, examined in its clean linked worktree standing at exactly that head. What I reproduced myself: go test ./internal/apphost/ -run TestUpdateConfig -count=1 at this head passes all four tests with exit 0 (preserves concurrent custody, no-change writes nothing, mutate error leaves file unchanged, creates from base when no file exists), corroborating the gates recorded in the artifacts. What I accepted after reading the diff and the recorded evidence: Architecture - affected layers are internal/apphost, internal/app, and docs/reference/architecture.md, and their contracts are preserved: UpdateConfig holds one exclusive advisory lock across the whole load-modify-store and merges only caller-declared fields onto a fresh reload; first publication stays on the exclusive hard-link create path outside the update contract; platforms without advisory locking refuse updates loudly while first publication remains available; the architecture page separates the four custody paths it previously conflated, including in-memory versus on-disk locks, updated in this same head. Security - .config.lock is an empty 0600 file beside the protected file, never renamed, released by the kernel when a process dies, so no stale lock survives a crash; both the reload and the store happen inside LOCK_EX so no lock-respecting process can interleave between them; a mutate error or a no-change update rewrites nothing and leaves file and workspace view unchanged; refused updates land nothing locally; no secret is exposed by the lock file. Bounds under concurrent writers hold: creators serialise behind the same lock and merge rather than overwrite. Simplification - no opportunity found worth requesting; the lock shims and the merge helper are already minimal. Filed by hand resting on the request, my promise, and all three exact-head artifacts.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:cbb6cc9b32b2db6f9f2137dbf2acdd4d1e979927","branch":"request/custody-lost-update-current","head":"85bb57b0c396c81f488a7acb457467cad6d1d887","verdict":"approved"}}